            <ArticleTitle>3-Oxo-2-piperazinyl acetamides as potent bradykinin B1 receptor antagonists for the treatment of pain and inflammation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3384-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2011.03.115</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The discovery of novel and highly potent oxopiperazine based B1 receptor antagonists is described. Compared to the previously described arylsulfonylated (R)-3-amino-3-phenylpropionic acid series, the current compounds showed improved in vitro potency and metabolic stability. Compound 17, 2-((2R)-1-((4-methylphenyl)sulfonyl)-3-oxo-2-piperazinyl)-N-((1R)-6-(1-piperidinylmethyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-1-naphthalenyl)acetamide, showed EC(50) of 10.3 nM in a rabbit biochemical challenge model. The practical syntheses of chiral arylsulfonylated oxopiperazine acetic acids are also described.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2011 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
